            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0154" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/10–2549: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-25">October 25,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received November 10—2:40 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–336. Re: Embassy telegram No. 1144, September 13, 1949. During conversation
                    with an Embassy officer on October 24, President <pb facs="0155" n="145"
                        xml:id="pg145"/> Rhee expressed great concern at possible recognition of
                    communist China by the United Kingdom or at possible attempts by Northwest
                    Airlines to land in communist-held China.</p>
                <p>Dr. Rhee said that if the United Kingdom should recognize communist China he
                    thought that his Government would have to sever diplomatic relations with the
                    United Kingdom. He said the big democratic countries could afford to temporize
                    with the communists, but Korea could not; Korea had “burned her bridges” and
                    intended to oppose the communists without compromise.</p>
                <p>As regards rumors he had heard that Northwest Airlines was considering securing
                    landing rights in Tientsin or Peiping, President Rhee said that if NWA tried to
                    land in Chinese communist territory after using Kimpo Airport as an intermediary
                    landing point, he would find it necessary to cancel existing landing rights of
                    NWA in Korea.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
